Screenline Comparison
Screenlines aggregate volumes across every facility crossing a corridor into one crossing total, smoothing out segment-level count noise for a bigger-picture check on the model’s overall travel pattern by corridor. Modeled totals come straight from the TDM’s own per-run Summary_Screenline.csv (built by summing Summary_SEGID.csv up to each ScreenlineID via a segment-to-screenline crosswalk, both produced fresh every run). Observed totals reuse the same 2023 AADT-based target built for the VMT comparison above, aggregated up to screenline level via that same crosswalk, then split across AM/MD/PM/EV using the model’s own period shares (the raw CCS-derived observed data is daily-only).






